//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// Broadening Formation — #TheStrat
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A broadening formation is what a market expanding in BOTH directions looks
// like: a higher high, then a lower low, then a higher high again, then a lower
// low again — a megaphone. In #TheStrat it is the structure that gives a trade
// its magnitude. Actionable signals are measured to "the previous broadening
// formation point": the last place the other side of the market actually
// defended.
//
// WHAT COUNTS AS A FORMATION
//   Points are swing pivots that strictly alternate high, low, high, low ... A
//   same-side pivot that prints before the other side does is merged into the
//   more extreme of the two, so the sequence can never repeat a side.
//
//   Points 1 and 2 are the seed — the first high and the first low, no
//   condition attached. From point 3 on, every point must EXPAND on the point
//   two back:
//
//       point 3 > point 1     (higher high)
//       point 4 < point 2     (lower low)
//       point 5 > point 3     (higher high)
//       ...
//
//   The chain runs for as long as that holds. The first pivot that fails to
//   expand ends the formation, and that failed pivot together with the one
//   before it becomes the seed of the next one. The formation on screen is
//   therefore always the longest run of consecutive expansions ending at the
//   most recent pivot.
//
//   Three points is the earliest the structure can be called: the seed high and
//   low, then the first point that expands on one of them. Only one side has
//   expanded at that stage, so the other side still has a single point and its
//   rail is drawn flat through it — there is no second point yet to give it a
//   slope. It picks up its slope the moment point 4 prints. Four points is the
//   first count that is broadening on both sides, five the classic count where
//   the outside-in trade is taken.
//
// WHAT IS DRAWN
//   * THE RAILS — the expanding edges. Each rail is anchored on the most recent
//     point of its own side and sloped so that every earlier point of that side
//     sits inside it: the containing trendline a chartist would draw by hand.
//     A side holding only one point so far is drawn flat through it. Rails
//     project forward, so the edge of the range is visible where it is NOW, not
//     only where it was.
//   * THE BODY between the rails, shaded.
//   * THE LEGS — the real price path 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> ... inside the megaphone.
//   * NUMBERED POINTS, each carrying in its tooltip the Strat type of the bar
//     that made it (1, 2u, 2d, 3) and the price.
//   * MAGNITUDE and INVALIDATION for the live read (below).
//   * RAIL TAGS — bars that trade into a projected rail, where the outside-in
//     entry lives.
//
//   Finished formations stay on the chart, trimmed and frozen, so the sequence
//   of expansions and where each one stopped is readable at a glance.
//
// THE TRADE THE STRUCTURE OFFERS
//   Broadening formations are traded from the outside in. When the newest point
//   is a high, price has just probed the top rail and failed; the rotation that
//   follows targets the opposite side, and the magnitude of that rotation is
//   the previous point — the last low. The formation's own extreme is the
//   invalidation: taken out, the expansion simply continued and that high is
//   now the next point of a longer formation.
//
//       newest point is a HIGH -> magnitude = previous LOW,  invalid above it
//       newest point is a LOW  -> magnitude = previous HIGH, invalid below it
//
//   ROTATION RATE in the dashboard measures exactly that, on the symbol and
//   timeframe in front of you: of every point this script has confirmed, how
//   often price reached the opposite point before taking out the point's own
//   extreme. Measurement starts at the bar the pivot is CONFIRMED — left+right
//   bars after the fact — not at the pivot itself, so it counts only what was
//   tradeable in real time. A bar that does both at once cannot be resolved
//   without intrabar data; those are counted as ambiguous and excluded from the
//   rate rather than guessed at.
//
// NOTE ON PIVOT STRENGTH
//   Left/right = 1 gives the raw bar-by-bar structure — every 2u that gets
//   reversed is a point. Larger values step back to swing structure and print
//   fewer, bigger formations. The right-hand setting is also the lag: a point
//   cannot be known until that many bars have closed after it.
// =============================================================================

indicator("Broadening Formation #TheStrat", "BF", overlay = true,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ================================== Inputs ===================================
gStr = "Structure"
pivLeft  = input.int(2, "Pivot strength   left", minval = 1, maxval = 25, group = gStr, inline = "piv")
pivRight = input.int(2, "right", minval = 1, maxval = 25, group = gStr, inline = "piv",
     tooltip = "Bars either side of a swing needed to call it a point. Left/right = 1 is the raw bar-by-bar structure; higher values give fewer, larger formations. Right is also the confirmation lag.")
minPts   = input.int(3, "Minimum points", minval = 3, maxval = 10, group = gStr,
     tooltip = "How many alternating, expanding points before the formation is drawn. 3 = the seed high and low plus the first expansion off one of them — the side that has not expanded yet gets a flat rail through its single point until it does. 4 = one expansion on each side. 5 = the classic count where the outside-in trade is taken.")

gDraw = "Formation"
showRails = input.bool(true, "Rails", group = gDraw, inline = "rail")
railWidth = input.int(2, "W", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = gDraw, inline = "rail")
railStyIn = input.string("Solid", "", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], group = gDraw, inline = "rail")
upCol     = input.color(color.rgb(239, 83, 80), "Upper", group = gDraw, inline = "col")
dnCol     = input.color(color.rgb(38, 166, 154), "Lower", group = gDraw, inline = "col")
showFill  = input.bool(true, "Shade body", group = gDraw, inline = "fill")
bodyCol   = input.color(color.rgb(120, 123, 134), "", group = gDraw, inline = "fill")
fillTrans = input.int(92, "Transp", minval = 50, maxval = 100, group = gDraw, inline = "fill")
showLegs  = input.bool(true, "Legs (price path through the points)", group = gDraw, inline = "leg")
legCol    = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 30), "", group = gDraw, inline = "leg")
showPts   = input.bool(true, "Numbered points", group = gDraw, inline = "pt")
lblSizeIn = input.string("small", "", options = ["tiny", "small", "normal"], group = gDraw, inline = "pt")
projBars  = input.int(20, "Project rails forward (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 200, group = gDraw)
keepForms = input.int(3, "Finished formations kept", minval = 0, maxval = 10, group = gDraw,
     tooltip = "0 keeps only the live formation on the chart.")

gLvl = "Magnitude / invalidation"
showLvls = input.bool(true, "Show levels off the newest point", group = gLvl)
tgtCol   = input.color(color.rgb(255, 193, 7), "Magnitude", group = gLvl, inline = "lv")
invCol   = input.color(color.rgb(156, 39, 176), "Invalidation", group = gLvl, inline = "lv")
showTags = input.bool(true, "Mark bars that tag a projected rail", group = gLvl,
     tooltip = "The outside-in entry: price trading back into the expanding edge of the formation.")

gTbl = "Dashboard"
showTbl = input.bool(true, "Show dashboard", group = gTbl)
tblPos  = input.string("top_right", "Position", options = ["top_right", "top_left", "bottom_right", "bottom_left", "middle_right"], group = gTbl)
posSel  = tblPos == "top_left" ? position.top_left : tblPos == "bottom_right" ? position.bottom_right : tblPos == "bottom_left" ? position.bottom_left : tblPos == "middle_right" ? position.middle_right : position.top_right

f_style(string s) => s == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : s == "Dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid
railStyle = f_style(railStyIn)
lblSize   = lblSizeIn == "tiny" ? size.tiny : lblSizeIn == "normal" ? size.normal : size.small

// ================================== Types ====================================
// One confirmed pivot: its price, the bar it printed on, which side it is, and
// the Strat type of that bar (1 / 2u / 2d / 3).
type Pt
    float  p
    int    b
    bool   hi
    string t

// A finished formation's drawings, kept whole so the whole set can be recycled
// together once it falls out of the "formations kept" window.
type Draw
    array<line>     lines
    array<label>    labels
    array<linefill> fills

// One point being measured for the rotation rate: does price reach the opposite
// point (tgt) before taking out the point's own extreme (inv)?
type Pend
    float tgt
    float inv
    bool  down

// ================================ Pivot chain ================================
var array<Pt> pts = array.new<Pt>()

f_barType(int off) =>
    bool up = high[off] > high[off + 1]
    bool dn = low[off]  < low[off + 1]
    up and dn ? "3" : up ? "2u" : dn ? "2d" : "1"

// Append a pivot, keeping the sequence strictly alternating. A pivot on the
// same side as the last one does not add a point — it either replaces it (if it
// is the more extreme of the two) or is discarded, because until the other side
// prints there has been no rotation.
f_addPt(float price, int b, bool hi, string t) =>
    bool changed = false
    int  n = array.size(pts)
    if n == 0
        array.push(pts, Pt.new(price, b, hi, t))
        changed := true
    else
        Pt last = array.get(pts, n - 1)
        if last.hi == hi
            if (hi and price > last.p) or (not hi and price < last.p)
                last.p := price
                last.b := b
                last.t := t
                changed := true
        else
            array.push(pts, Pt.new(price, b, hi, t))
            changed := true
    changed

// Does point i expand on the point two back — the last one on its own side?
f_expands(int i) =>
    Pt c = array.get(pts, i)
    Pt r = array.get(pts, i - 2)
    c.hi ? c.p > r.p : c.p < r.p

// Walk back from the newest point for as long as each one expands. The chain
// stops at the first failure; the two points before that failure are the seed
// of the run, so the start is one further back than the last expanding point.
f_chainStart() =>
    int n = array.size(pts)
    int j = n - 1
    if n >= 3
        for k = n - 1 to 2
            if f_expands(k)
                j := k - 1
            else
                break
    j - 1 < 0 ? 0 : j - 1

// ============================== Rotation record ==============================
// Resolved BEFORE this bar's pivots are processed, so a point registered on bar
// N is first measured on bar N+1 — never on the bar that revealed it.
var array<Pend> pend = array.new<Pend>()
var int rotHit = 0
var int rotMiss = 0
var int rotAmb  = 0

if array.size(pend) > 0
    for i = array.size(pend) - 1 to 0
        Pend q = array.get(pend, i)
        bool hit = q.down ? low <= q.tgt : high >= q.tgt
        bool inv = q.down ? high > q.inv : low < q.inv
        if hit and inv
            rotAmb += 1
            array.remove(pend, i)
        else if hit
            rotHit += 1
            array.remove(pend, i)
        else if inv
            rotMiss += 1
            array.remove(pend, i)

// ================================ Drawing state ==============================
var array<line>     curLines  = array.new<line>()
var array<label>    curLabels = array.new<label>()
var array<linefill> curFills  = array.new<linefill>()
var array<Draw>     hist      = array.new<Draw>()

var line  upRail = na
var line  dnRail = na
var line  tgtLn  = na
var line  invLn  = na
var label tgtLb  = na
var label invLb  = na

// Rails are stored as anchor + slope so they can be re-projected on every bar
// without rebuilding the formation.
var float upSlope = na
var int   upAnchB = na
var float upAnchP = na
var float dnSlope = na
var int   dnAnchB = na
var float dnAnchP = na

var int   drawnStart = na     // bar of point 1 of the formation on screen
var bool  curLive    = false  // is that formation still the live chain?
var int   curCount   = 0
var int   curLastBar = na
var bool  curLastHi  = false
var float curTgt     = na
var float curInv     = na
var int   regBar     = na     // last point already entered in the rotation record

f_clearLive() =>
    line.delete(tgtLn)
    line.delete(invLn)
    label.delete(tgtLb)
    label.delete(invLb)

// =============================== Pivot intake ================================
float ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pivLeft, pivRight)
float pl = ta.pivotlow(low, pivLeft, pivRight)

bool ptsChanged = false
if not na(ph)
    bool addedHi = f_addPt(ph, bar_index - pivRight, true, f_barType(pivRight))
    ptsChanged := ptsChanged or addedHi
if not na(pl)
    bool addedLo = f_addPt(pl, bar_index - pivRight, false, f_barType(pivRight))
    ptsChanged := ptsChanged or addedLo

if array.size(pts) > 300
    array.shift(pts)

bool newForm  = false
bool newPoint = false
bool formEnd  = false

// ========================= Formation build / rebuild =========================
if ptsChanged and array.size(pts) >= 2
    int n    = array.size(pts)
    int s    = f_chainStart()
    int sBar = array.get(pts, s).b
    int cnt  = n - s

    // The live chain has moved off the formation on screen: that one is done.
    if curLive and sBar != drawnStart
        curLive := false
        formEnd := true
        f_clearLive()
        tgtLn := na
        invLn := na
        tgtLb := na
        invLb := na

    if cnt >= minPts
        bool isNew = na(drawnStart) or sBar != drawnStart

        // A genuinely different formation: freeze the old drawing set, trimmed
        // back to its own last point so dead rails do not run across the chart.
        if isNew and not na(drawnStart)
            int trimX = curLastBar + (projBars < 10 ? projBars : 10)
            if not na(upRail)
                line.set_x2(upRail, trimX)
                line.set_y2(upRail, upAnchP + upSlope * (trimX - upAnchB))
            if not na(dnRail)
                line.set_x2(dnRail, trimX)
                line.set_y2(dnRail, dnAnchP + dnSlope * (trimX - dnAnchB))
            array.push(hist, Draw.new(curLines, curLabels, curFills))
            curLines  := array.new<line>()
            curLabels := array.new<label>()
            curFills  := array.new<linefill>()
            upRail := na
            dnRail := na
            if array.size(hist) > keepForms
                Draw old = array.shift(hist)
                for fl in old.fills
                    linefill.delete(fl)
                for ln in old.lines
                    line.delete(ln)
                for lb in old.labels
                    label.delete(lb)

        // Same formation, one point longer (or a point that moved): redraw it.
        for ln in curLines
            line.delete(ln)
        array.clear(curLines)
        for lb in curLabels
            label.delete(lb)
        array.clear(curLabels)
        for fl in curFills
            linefill.delete(fl)
        array.clear(curFills)
        upRail := na
        dnRail := na
        f_clearLive()
        tgtLn := na
        invLn := na
        tgtLb := na
        invLb := na

        // ---- the newest point on each side, which anchors that side's rail ---
        int   hiLastB = na
        float hiLastP = na
        int   loLastB = na
        float loLastP = na
        for i = s to n - 1
            Pt q = array.get(pts, i)
            if q.hi
                hiLastB := q.b
                hiLastP := q.p
            else
                loLastB := q.b
                loLastP := q.p

        // ---- rails: anchored on the newest point of the side, sloped so that
        //      every earlier point of that side is contained --------------------
        float upS = na
        float dnS = na
        for i = s to n - 1
            Pt q = array.get(pts, i)
            if q.hi and q.b < hiLastB
                float slU = (hiLastP - q.p) / (hiLastB - q.b)
                upS := na(upS) ? slU : math.min(upS, slU)
            if not q.hi and q.b < loLastB
                float slD = (loLastP - q.p) / (loLastB - q.b)
                dnS := na(dnS) ? slD : math.max(dnS, slD)
        upSlope := na(upS) ? 0.0 : upS
        dnSlope := na(dnS) ? 0.0 : dnS
        upAnchB := hiLastB
        upAnchP := hiLastP
        dnAnchB := loLastB
        dnAnchP := loLastP

        int xL   = array.get(pts, s).b
        int xEnd = hiLastB > loLastB ? hiLastB : loLastB
        int xR   = (bar_index > xEnd ? bar_index : xEnd) + projBars

        if showRails
            upRail := line.new(xL, upAnchP + upSlope * (xL - upAnchB), xR, upAnchP + upSlope * (xR - upAnchB),
                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = upCol, style = railStyle, width = railWidth)
            dnRail := line.new(xL, dnAnchP + dnSlope * (xL - dnAnchB), xR, dnAnchP + dnSlope * (xR - dnAnchB),
                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = dnCol, style = railStyle, width = railWidth)
            array.push(curLines, upRail)
            array.push(curLines, dnRail)
            if showFill
                array.push(curFills, linefill.new(upRail, dnRail, color.new(bodyCol, fillTrans)))

        // ---- legs: the path price actually took between the points ----------
        if showLegs
            for i = s to n - 2
                Pt legA = array.get(pts, i)
                Pt legB = array.get(pts, i + 1)
                array.push(curLines, line.new(legA.b, legA.p, legB.b, legB.p, xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                     color = legCol, style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))

        // ---- numbered points ------------------------------------------------
        if showPts
            for i = s to n - 1
                Pt q = array.get(pts, i)
                int num = i - s + 1
                string what = num <= 2 ? (q.hi ? "high" : "low") : (q.hi ? "higher high" : "lower low")
                array.push(curLabels, label.new(q.b, q.p, str.tostring(num), xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                     yloc = yloc.price,
                     style = q.hi ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
                     color = color.new(q.hi ? upCol : dnCol, 25),
                     textcolor = color.white, size = lblSize,
                     tooltip = "Point " + str.tostring(num) + " — " + what + "\n" +
                         str.tostring(q.p, format.mintick) + "   Strat bar: " + q.t))

        // ---- the live read off the newest point ------------------------------
        Pt lastPt = array.get(pts, n - 1)
        Pt prevPt = array.get(pts, n - 2)
        curTgt    := prevPt.p
        curInv    := lastPt.p
        curLastHi := lastPt.hi

        if showLvls
            tgtLn := line.new(lastPt.b, curTgt, xR, curTgt, xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                 color = tgtCol, style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)
            invLn := line.new(lastPt.b, curInv, xR, curInv, xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                 color = invCol, style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            tgtLb := label.new(xR, curTgt, "Magnitude  " + str.tostring(curTgt, format.mintick),
                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left,
                 color = color.new(tgtCol, 85), textcolor = tgtCol, size = size.small)
            invLb := label.new(xR, curInv, "Invalid  " + str.tostring(curInv, format.mintick),
                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left,
                 color = color.new(invCol, 85), textcolor = invCol, size = size.small)

        newForm    := isNew
        newPoint   := not isNew and cnt > curCount
        drawnStart := sBar
        curCount   := cnt
        curLastBar := lastPt.b
        curLive    := true

        // Enter the newest point in the rotation record once, from the bar it
        // was confirmed on.
        if na(regBar) or lastPt.b != regBar
            array.push(pend, Pend.new(curTgt, curInv, lastPt.hi))
            regBar := lastPt.b
            if array.size(pend) > 50
                array.shift(pend)

// ========================= Live projection & rail tags =======================
float upNow = curLive and not na(upAnchP) ? upAnchP + upSlope * (bar_index - upAnchB) : na
float dnNow = curLive and not na(dnAnchP) ? dnAnchP + dnSlope * (bar_index - dnAnchB) : na

if barstate.islast and curLive
    int xR = bar_index + projBars
    if not na(upRail)
        line.set_x2(upRail, xR)
        line.set_y2(upRail, upAnchP + upSlope * (xR - upAnchB))
    if not na(dnRail)
        line.set_x2(dnRail, xR)
        line.set_y2(dnRail, dnAnchP + dnSlope * (xR - dnAnchB))
    if not na(tgtLn)
        line.set_x2(tgtLn, xR)
        label.set_x(tgtLb, xR)
    if not na(invLn)
        line.set_x2(invLn, xR)
        label.set_x(invLb, xR)

// A bar trading into the projected edge of a live formation — where the
// outside-in entry sits.
bool tagUp = showTags and curLive and not na(upNow) and bar_index > curLastBar and high >= upNow
bool tagDn = showTags and curLive and not na(dnNow) and bar_index > curLastBar and low <= dnNow

plotshape(tagUp, "Upper rail tag", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color = upCol, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(tagDn, "Lower rail tag", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color = dnCol, size = size.tiny)

// ================================ Dashboard ==================================
var table dash = table.new(posSel, 2, 10, border_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 50), frame_width = 1)

f_row(int r, string k, string v, color vc) =>
    table.cell(dash, 0, r, k, text_color = color.new(color.gray, 10), text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(dash, 1, r, v, text_color = vc, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_right)

if showTbl and barstate.islast
    int    resolved = rotHit + rotMiss
    string rotTxt   = resolved == 0 ? "—" :
         str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * rotHit / resolved)) + "%  (n=" + str.tostring(resolved) +
         (rotAmb > 0 ? ", " + str.tostring(rotAmb) + " amb" : "") + ")"
    color  headCol  = not curLive ? color.gray : curLastHi ? upCol : dnCol
    string state    = na(drawnStart) ? "none yet" : curLive ? str.tostring(curCount) + " points — live" : str.tostring(curCount) + " points — ended"
    float  span     = na(upNow) or na(dnNow) ? na : upNow - dnNow
    float  loc      = na(span) or span <= 0 ? na : 100.0 * (close - dnNow) / span

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "BROADENING FORMATION", text_color = headCol, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, timeframe.period, text_color = headCol, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_right)
    f_row(1, "Formation", state, curLive ? color.white : color.gray)
    f_row(2, "Newest point", not curLive ? "—" : "P" + str.tostring(curCount) + " " + (curLastHi ? "high" : "low") + "  " + str.tostring(curInv, format.mintick), curLive ? headCol : color.gray)
    f_row(3, "Rotation to", not curLive ? "—" : curLastHi ? "the lower rail" : "the upper rail", curLive ? color.white : color.gray)
    f_row(4, "Magnitude", curLive and not na(curTgt) ? str.tostring(curTgt, format.mintick) : "—", tgtCol)
    f_row(5, "Invalidation", curLive and not na(curInv) ? str.tostring(curInv, format.mintick) : "—", invCol)
    f_row(6, "Upper rail now", na(upNow) ? "—" : str.tostring(upNow, format.mintick), upCol)
    f_row(7, "Lower rail now", na(dnNow) ? "—" : str.tostring(dnNow, format.mintick), dnCol)
    f_row(8, "Price in range", na(loc) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(loc)) + "%", color.white)
    f_row(9, "Rotation rate", rotTxt, resolved == 0 ? color.gray : color.white)

// ================================== Alerts ===================================
alertcondition(newForm,  "Broadening formation formed",
     "A broadening formation has completed its minimum point count on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(newPoint, "Broadening formation extended",
     "The broadening formation on {{ticker}} {{interval}} has added a point — the range expanded again.")
alertcondition(formEnd,  "Broadening formation ended",
     "A pivot failed to expand: the broadening formation on {{ticker}} {{interval}} is finished.")
alertcondition(tagUp,    "Upper rail tagged",
     "Price is trading into the upper rail of the broadening formation on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(tagDn,    "Lower rail tagged",
     "Price is trading into the lower rail of the broadening formation on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if newForm or newPoint
    alert("Broadening formation " + (newForm ? "formed" : "extended") + " on " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period +
         ": point " + str.tostring(curCount) + " is a " + (curLastHi ? "higher high" : "lower low") + " at " +
         str.tostring(curInv, format.mintick) + ". Rotation " + (curLastHi ? "down" : "up") + " to " +
         str.tostring(curTgt, format.mintick) + "; the expansion simply continues if that point gives way.",
         alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
